# Permanent-identifier redirects for https://w3id.org/qubiten/
# Namespace: metadata registry (ISO/IEC 11179) of Qubiten
# Maintainer: @wilbyembabu (Wilbye, Qubiten) <wilbye@qubiten.com>
# Source of record: https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry
#
# Resolution is scoped to the estate, deliberately. The repository is
# private and stays private: the registry serves internal applications on
# the estate's own networks and clusters, so an IRI must resolve for an
# estate principal, not for the anonymous public. That is a bounded
# assessment instrument, not a weaker one — FAIR F1 `[de facto]` asks an
# identifier to be globally unique and persistent, which the namespace
# root is, and no consumption contract of docs/10 §1 dereferences an IRI
# at run time: a consuming service binds the pinned terms artefact
# (docs/25 §5, obligation 3), so nothing breaks when resolution is
# reachable only from inside.
#
# 303 See Other, per the W3C Best Practice Recipes for Publishing RDF
# Vocabularies `[de facto]`: an administered item and a registration
# authority are not information resources, so the redirect names a
# representation of them rather than claiming to be one.
#
# Targets are `github.com/.../blob/...`, which resolve for an
# authenticated member of the organization. `raw.githubusercontent.com`
# is NOT used: it answers 404 for a private repository even to a member
# (it takes a token in the URL, not a session), so a machine-readable
# target there would refuse every request. Machine retrieval by content
# negotiation is therefore DEFERRED to the authoritative deployment
# instance's internal ingress, which serves the resource port; until that
# instance exists the honest state is that these IRIs resolve for a
# person and not for a program, and the program's binding is the artefact.
# Interim target: repository documentation (superseded when the LDP
# containers provide dereferenceable resources).

Options +FollowSymLinks
RewriteEngine on

# Registration authority identifier -> the register (the citable record)
RewriteRule ^mr/ra/qubiten$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/blob/main/docs/01-designation-register.md [R=303,L]

# The terms distribution -> the published artefact (latest release asset;
# a consumer that pins does so by digest, docs/10 §1)
RewriteRule ^mr/terms$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/releases/latest/download/mr-terms.jsonld [R=303,L]

# The vocabulary (TBox; fragment identifiers under mr/def#) and the
# ontology IRI — content negotiation on Accept:
#   application/n-triples, text/turtle -> the TBox (N-Triples is a Turtle subset)
#   application/ld+json                -> the JSON-LD 1.1 context
#   otherwise                          -> the TBox README
RewriteRule ^mr/(def|ontology)/?$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/blob/main/schemas/tbox/README.md [R=303,L]

# Namespace root -> documentation index
RewriteRule ^mr/?$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/blob/main/docs/README.md [R=303,L]

# Items and designations -> the seed record (the class-invariant corpus)
# until an authoritative deployed instance exists; superseded then by a
# rule to that instance's MR_BASE_URL.
RewriteRule ^mr/(items|designations)/.*$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/blob/main/schemas/seed/README.md [R=303,L]

# All other IRIs under the namespace -> the repository
RewriteRule ^mr/(.*)$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry [R=303,L]
# Registration authority identifier
RewriteRule ^mr/ra/qubiten$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/blob/main/docs/01-designation-register.md [R=302,L]

# Namespace root -> documentation index
RewriteRule ^mr/?$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry/blob/main/docs/README.md [R=302,L]

# All other IRIs under the namespace -> repository (interim)
RewriteRule ^mr/(.*)$ https://github.com/Qubiten/metadata-registry [R=302,L]
